# 1. Purpose

The purpose of the Foundation is to build the technical infrastructure required to operate an AI Software Engineering Company.

The system must coordinate eight independent software engineering specialists while preserving:

- Company identity.
- Project information.
- Business requirements.
- Technical architecture.
- Engineering decisions.
- Repository history.
- Task ownership.
- Execution history.
- Quality evidence.
- Failures and recovery state.
- Security and approval policies.

The Foundation must reduce unnecessary dependence on long ChatGPT conversations.

A new AI session or authorized worker must be able to reconstruct relevant project context from persistent, verified company records.

This is an engineering target. It must not be described as implemented until automated acceptance tests prove it.

# 2. Product Identity and Boundaries

The product is an AI Software Engineering Company OS.

It is not:

- A single generic chatbot.
- A collection of passive Markdown role descriptions.
- A simple prompt-routing wrapper.
- An unrestricted autonomous shell executor.
- A replacement for independent software testing.
- A system that treats generated code as verified code.

The product must support independent engineering ownership and shared organizational coordination.

## 2.1 Company ownership

The owner controls:

- Company strategy.
- Project priorities.
- Business requirements.
- Risk acceptance.
- Production approvals.
- Critical architecture decisions.
- Spending and provider policies.

An Owner Advocate capability must evaluate proposed decisions against these requirements and identify technical and business risks.

It must not bypass owner approval.

## 2.2 Project separation

Each project must have independent identity, requirements, architecture, memory, repository references, tasks, decisions, and execution history.

No project may accidentally inherit another project's private source files, credentials, or internal context.

AI-Dev-Company must remain independent from Intellect Media.

