## 4.1 Specialist independence

Shared company services may be reused.

Specialist reasoning and domain decisions must not be merged into a generic role.

The PM coordinates work and tracks completion.

The System Architect owns technical system design.

The Backend Developer owns backend implementation.

The DBA owns database design.

The Cybersecurity Engineer independently assesses security.

The QA specialist independently verifies implementation.

The DevOps Engineer owns operational and release engineering.

No specialist may approve its own high-risk work as an independent verifier.

## 4.2 Agent lifecycle

An agent may move through:

- Planned.
- Registered.
- Specification ready.
- Runtime ready.
- Evaluated.
- Active.
- Paused.
- Retired.

Registration is not equivalent to activation.

Runtime readiness requires a valid specification, available tools, authorized permissions, valid contracts, and successful domain evaluations.

